  "text": "Python typing got fast enough to feel invisible. PyreFly is a new open source type checker and IDE language server from Meta written in Rust with a focus on instant feedback and real-world developer experience. Today we dig into what it is, why it exists, and how it plays with the rest of the Python typing ecosystem. We have Abby Mitchell, Danny Yang, and Kyle Inteau from PyreFly here to dive into the project. This is Talk Python to Me, episode 523, recorded September 9th, 2025."
